# Neutrino masses

A short demo of the rendered HTML post with enough content to inspect the page theme, including a blockquote, math and a code sample.

> The absolute mass scale is still unknown; oscillation only fixes the splittings.

## Oscillation evidence

- solar and reactor experiments
- atmospheric and long-baseline beams

Inline math such as $ m_\nu \lesssim 0.1\ \mathrm{eV} $ sits in the text.

Block math:

$ \Delta m^2_{21} \approx 7.5 \times 10^{-5}\ \mathrm{eV}^2 $

```python
import numpy as np

def splittings(m):
    return np.diff(m ** 2)
```

